<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Counting solutions from a sketch</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(f(x) = {@f@}\).</p><p>(a) Find the \(y\)-coordinate of the maximum point and of the minimum point of \(y = f(x)\).</p><div>Maximum point: \(y =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>Minimum point: \(y =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(b) How many real solutions has the equation \(f(x) = {@kq@}\)?</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(c) The equation \(f(x) = c\) has three real solutions when</p><div>[[input:ans4]] \(\lt c \lt\) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans4]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(f'(x) = {@df@} = {@3*a0*(x-p0)*(x-q0)@}\), which is \(0\) at \(x = {@p0@}\) and \(x = {@q0@}\). The leading coefficient is positive, so the curve rises, turns at the maximum point \(({@p0@}, {@ymax@})\), falls to the minimum point \(({@q0@}, {@ymin@})\) and rises again.</p><p>(b) The solutions of \(f(x) = {@kq@}\) are where the line \(y = {@kq@}\) meets the curve. [[if test="is(ns=3)"]]The line lies between the minimum and maximum values, so it meets the curve three times.[[else]][[if test="is(ns=1)"]]The line lies [[if test="is(hi=1)"]]above the maximum[[else]]below the minimum[[/if]] value, so it meets the curve once.[[else]]The line passes through a turning point, where it touches the curve, and crosses the curve once more: two solutions.[[/if]][[/if]]</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Sketch of y = f(x) with a maximum point at ({#p0#}, {#ymax#}) and a minimum point at ({#q0#}, {#ymin#}), and the dashed line y = {#kq#}, which meets the curve {#ns#} times.">
[[jsxgraph width="360px" height="280px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [{#xl#}, {#yu+pd#}, {#xr#}, {#yl-pd#}], axis: true, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  // the curve and the line y = k
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x) { return {#a0#}*x*x*x+({#coeff(f,x,2)#})*x*x+({#coeff(f,x,1)#})*x+({#d0#}); }], {strokeColor: '#1f4e9c', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('line', [[0, {#kq#}], [1, {#kq#}]], {strokeColor: '#000000', dash: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('point', [{#p0#}, {#ymax#}], {name: '({#p0#}, {#ymax#})', size: 3, fixed: true, strokeColor: '#000000', fillColor: '#000000', showInfobox: false, label: {useMathJax: false, offset: [8, 8]}});
  b.create('point', [{#q0#}, {#ymin#}], {name: '({#q0#}, {#ymin#})', size: 3, fixed: true, strokeColor: '#000000', fillColor: '#000000', showInfobox: false, label: {useMathJax: false, offset: [8, -14]}});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div><p>(c) Three solutions need the line strictly between the minimum and maximum values: \({@ymin@} \lt c \lt {@ymax@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
